{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them","id":1419152,"title":"Tolerating Vampires, reasons to, Magick tactics and infiltrating them","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-20T06:01:03-07:00","id":1419152,"title":"Tolerating Vampires, reasons to, Magick tactics and infiltrating them","content":"Last night was a harrowing ordeal. We went to a Hollow One bar only to find it infested with thirsty Vampires. They wanted Our magick blood and weren't taking no for an answer. The Hermetic projected an illusion of a bond-fire into their minds, sending them into Rostrecht. We tracked them to their lair. The first rays of sun now light the horizon. If we show mercy, do we become their dinner?<br /> <br /> I don't include vampires in my Mage setting, because I find the masquerade hard to explain, especially given the Sabbat's efforts to break it. If you love Vampire crossover, these ideas have been collecting dust.<br /> <br /> There are a hundred and one ways to invade a vampire haven during the day if you have Sphere Magick. So why wouldn't a Cabal wipe them out?<br /> <br /> Reasons to Tolerate Vampires:<br /> - They have ghouls who will die without their blood.<br /> - Humankind is overbreeding and destroying the planet. An apex predator, above humans, is necessary.<br /> - Every vampire was once human and most were sought out by their sires, whatever their other plans might have been. They have a right to exist. <br /> - They are a problem for the Technocracy. OR, one only needs to capture video of a Tzimisce torture session and show it to the Celestial Chorus to keep the Traditions busy with them.<br /> <br /> Securing Lasting Peace:<br /> The Toreadore Clan of both sects love art. Mages with Correspondence, Matter, Forces, Entropy and Mind can create art that no vampire could hope to produce. They are easily impressed (entranced) with extra-dimensional art and that art fetches a high price.<br /> The Life Sphere can be used to generate large supplies of blood for vampires. <br /> <br /> Facilitating and Extending Magick through Blood Bonds - messing with ghouls:<br /> Ghouls are generally blood bound to a single Vampire. There are three common types of ghouls.<br /> 1. haven guards<br /> 2. institutional influence agents (the chief of police)<br /> 3. Sabbat war ghouls<br /> <br /> Before a human is turned into a ghoul, they have a set of important relationships to family, friends and paramours. People know them for who they are. If they have risen to a position of influence in an institution, it is usually because they are committed to fulfilling the mission statement of that organization. The relationship the person has to others and his sense of duty can be understood through the Spheres as part of a Societal Consensus. <br /> <br /> When a Vampire turns a human into a ghoul and blood bonds him, he fundamentally alters the ghoul's pattern of behavior and feelings toward others. All of a sudden, the Vampire's needs take priority over everyone and anything else. The Vampire doesn't need to compensate the ghoul with anything other than blood, an exchange that is done in secret. It is a sudden change that doesn't fit with the Consensus. Why has Jennifer moved to that windowless house, only to take calls for her ugly night-owl boyfriend? She had a great guy and lots of friends. Why is Captain Hills throwing homicide cases in the garbage?<br /> <br /> Mages have an agenda to advance their Paradigm and change the Consensus, at least locally. Vampires have an agenda to keep themselves hidden, to keep the masses from discovering and analyzing the mechanism of their influence. This is difficult in the information age. A ghoul's human family have an agenda to discover what has happened to their loved one. A smart Mage could plan an information sharing alliance with the family and friends of the ghoul that serves to advance their Paradigm and lay the foundation for all kinds of coincidental Magick.<br /> <br /> Step 1: Surveil the haven and record conversations between ghoul and master Keep most of the footage from ever being shown to anyone. Video record the ghoul leaving and returning from errands to prove where they are and who they are serving. <br /> <br /> Step 2: Approach Jennifer's family as a member of &quot;Champions of the Disappeared&quot;, a fringe activist group that investigates a secret society of kidnappers. Show the pictures of Jennifer coming and going from the haven. Duplicate that footage for different family members to stash, using this as a deterrent against vampiric aggression. Explain that some police may be involved in the conspiracy. You need lots of ordinary people working together to oppose the captor. <br /> <br /> The Vampire is completely vulnerable during the day and the ghoul can sense danger to their master through the blood bond. What if the ghoul IS the cause of danger to her beloved master? Her family now know where she is and are quite pissed at the owner of the windowless house. <br /> <br /> Step 3. Approach the ghoul during the day and explain what is going on. Emphasize that suicide to save the Vampire would only draw more attention to him, now that the relationship has been documented. Staying with the Vampire keeps the network of concerned people's attention on the haven. She needs to leave the haven but can't imagine going without that Vitae for great lengths of time. It is a weighty decision to consider. <br /> <br /> In the Scientific Consensus, it is believed that Stress manifests in the body in the form of frown-lines, grey hair, skin conditions and accelerated aging. Ghouls' bodies don't age and so can't resolve the stress superficially. Being a form of human, the ghoul has an average willpower of three, making Mind Effects on them easy, using the blood bond as a powerful anchor for effects. Induce massive mental stress on the ghoul using simple logic (Manipulation + Expression) and an difficulty-adjusted Mind spell. <br /> <br /> The stress of being the greatest source of danger to her one true love is going to manifest somewhere. Look into her psyche to determine if the stress will manifest as a behavioral disorder. Assuming you have a Cabal with most Spheres covered, checking her Prime Pattern and Spirit connections could yield valuable secrets applicable to Magick cast on ghouls. <br /> <br /> She is going to run home and talk to her master to warn him of the danger he is in. This is a perfect opportunity to use coincidental Magick on the Vampire from a distance, using her as the delivery system. Overwhelmed with the immediacy of the situation, she will go down during the day and wake him up, hitting him with Stress-Magick while he's weakened by the sun. Gods bless the sun! Now he can't sleep. He will consider killing the ghoul to cover his tracks before changing havens. The blood bond prevents her from seeing his monstrous intensions, delayed by the information network you have pointed at him. Each is aware that they are a danger to the other. Time for her to move out. <br /> <br /> On the trip home to her mom's, you offer up an explanation that can be used to focus attention away from the Vampire. Insert Mystic Paradigm Here. You are there to support her as she rebuilds her connection to family and friends. As time passes, the Stress Magick wears off, allowing her Pattern to readjust. Great time to study her Pattern further. Only one thing complicates her life. The feeling she has toward the Vampire is still stronger than any human connection she is trying to rebuild. <br /> <br /> You now have a group of believers, maybe even an Acolyte or two. You have a ghoul who is a psychic compass pointing at the Vampire. The range of possible effects that you could build on this connection is vast. So what about finding her a new source of Vitae? Since you saved the day, her family will assume she is safe with you. Time to hit that nightclub. In her Mind Pattern, the current blood bond distorts her image of the Regnant. This is supported by rationalizations forced also be the blood bond. The moment she meets a willing replacement is the time to cast more Magick, an effect that overlaps the end of the old blood bond and the beginning of the new one. <br /> <br /> The effect? Why not try to induce a form of polarized back-and-forth dual bond, creating alternately idealized and horrid images of each competing Regnant. If her image of the Regnants is fluid, you or another Mage could appear to take the form of that Regnant, giving false orders or debriefing her on masters' business. So, we've begun to climb the ladder, starting with the weakest connections, human to human, moving up to the all-powerful vampiric blood bond and have created a repeatable effect that can be used on a blood bound person.<br /> <br /> Vampires are people too. Disfavored Vampires get put down by princes for minor frenzies while an elder's closet full of atrocities goes unpunished. Princes are almost always blood bound to elder puppet masters who hide their influence, much like the Vampire who you just rescued the ghoul from. A Vampire Prince with high Perception, Empathy and sensory disciplines, like Auspex, is going to have a clear impression of the vile elder Regnant buried in his subconscious. The conflict between that and the idealized image created by his blood bond produces some fluidity. Pump in some Mind and Entropy and you can manifest to the Prince as this evil Elder and give false orders that expose the corruption. Dealing with Vampires Ahl-i-Batin style.<br /> <br /> Preemptive Infiltration, The Fate Weavers Way:<br /> Life Mages with many years ahead of them might take a longer view. Territory wars between Vampires happen often enough. Vampire societies have specific criteria for those they would embrace, often dictated by a strategic situation. Heavy hitters are need to vanquish the enemy. Socially adept society builders are needed to calm the population in the conquered territory. In addition to these criteria, individual Vampires select based on their own need, be it companionship or legacy. <br /> <br /> A little Time, Entropy and Mind could reveal who is on the short list for Vampiric Embrace. Why not cast effects on those candidates ahead of time that make them agents of your Cabal or Chantry. Once those agents are brought into the lower tier, use the above tactic to shake up the power pyramid, giving neonates early opportunities to move up the ranks. Diablery, the eating of a vampire's soul by another, is something to be understood through the Spirit and Prime Spheres. Since you're Cabal are going to be around, why not learn something from it? <br /> <br /> Claiming Vampire-Subverted Institutions:<br /> Captain Hills, the police chief is new on the job. He has a family. Kids have moved out and now it's just him and his wife. A seductive Sabbat Bishop takes him as a ghoul. A Vampire Pack under her jurisdiction has caused a ruckus, leaving grief-ridden mortals screaming for answers. Captain Hills wants to find the killers. The Bishop sends a currier with a letter asking him to meet her in private. At the meeting, she explains that the blood feasting rampage incident is being handled and revealing the killers' identities to the public would lead to a catastrophe. She would be put in personal danger. The Captain doesn't want anything bad to happen to her and he trusts her judgement. He proceeds to cover up the incident.<br /> <br /> Police officers undergo background checks. They are psychologically tested. Their actions and decisions are documented, forming a record that scientifically represents how that officer is likely to act in the future. A clever Mage need only surveil the captain and enlist others in the police and justice system to start a fact finding mission surrounding the Captain's sudden abandonment of previously demonstrated convictions. Insert Paradigm Here to hide the Bishop. Now, you have made some of your Magick coincidental to the police. City life just got easier for the Trads. <br /> <br /> When Chief Hills is finally confronted by your network of investigators, he will be made to realize he is a threat to his beloved Bishop. while he's trying to cover his bases at the station, approach his wife. Show her evidence of the relationship with the Bishop. It was not anything he was missing at home, but an Etherial Mystic Force that pushed him toward the seductress. Mrs. Hills can give you an understanding of how he related to a woman before being blood bound. You have a basis of comparison. A blood bond is a supernatural life altering effect without a publicly known explanation. The information void needed for vampires' survival is where you insert your paradigm to explain what is happening.<br /> <br /> Just as Magick has resonance, Vampiric Disciplines have psychic signatures. Who Dominated and memory wiped this witness? Study their Mind Pattern to discern the unique signature. Operating during the day, a Mage visiting an important local institution can stir up trouble that would force Vampires to leap into action the moment the sun sets. They would have to visit people who had gone home after their day-shift, using Presence and Dominate to thwart the plot set in motion by the Mage. This would keep the Vampires so busy, they would not have time to search for the Mage who is resting comfortably in his sensory deprivation tank in an undisclosed location. When other beings can create mind altering effects with no paradox and those beings die in sunlight, Mages have the incentive and time-window to force those beings' hand, building their paradigm on the unexplained. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T06:43:51-07:00","id":1419155,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s nice. I think the Verbrana would tolerate vampires, because it\u2019s not like they don\u2019t use tons of blood magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T07:45:25-07:00","id":1419160,"title":"","content":"Order of Hermes has entered chat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T16:34:41-07:00","id":1419259,"title":"","content":"Reasons to tolerate vampires:<br /> - You have plenty of enemies already. If you're already worrying about Technocrats, Nephandi, and Marauders, why piss off another established faction?<br /> - You probably don't know much about their abilities, fighting an unknown enemy is dangerous<br /> - If you can actually find a semi-trustworthy vampire, you could have a lot to offer each other, since you're probably good at very different things<br /> - Vampire mystics might have some fascinating lore that living magi haven't seen in ages<br /> - (if Hermetic) Those Tremere guys are basically just estranged cousins of the Order anyway, why not mend fences?<br /> <br /> Reasons not to tolerate vampires:<br /> - They prey on humans, that's just awful<br /> - They're not fully in control of themselves, even the ones who try to be nice-ish are liable to slip eventually, go into a frenzy and drain someone to death<br /> - They're habitual schemers, you probably can't trust them<br /> - (if Hermetic) Those Tremere bastards betrayed us all <i>and</i> they've been poaching our magi for centuries!<br /> <br /> I dunno. I always found it bizarre how oWoD books portrayed different supernaturals as being almost totally ignorant about each other. Being aware of another major supernatural faction and just ignoring them instead of either gathering information or trying to set up diplomatic talks seems odd. (Admittedly, those diplomatic talks might well end in &quot;let's agree to stay out of each other's business,&quot; but still.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T20:25:10-07:00","id":1419285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419259#post1419259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno. I always found it bizarre how oWoD books portrayed different supernaturals as being almost totally ignorant about each other. Being aware of another major supernatural faction and just ignoring them instead of either gathering information or trying to set up diplomatic talks seems odd. (Admittedly, those diplomatic talks might well end in &quot;let's agree to stay out of each other's business,&quot; but still.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess individual writers were focused on the internal logic of the game line they were writing for. If you are writing for a deadline, you want your imagination to generate rich plots with ancient seductive elders and the horror of Vampirism, not being forces to compare powers between a whole bunch of crossover. They did leave mixing open to the player-base. People seem to like crossover. I find including Wraith and Changeling in my Mage chronicle workable - &quot;Those other guys live in the Umbra. We should visit or commune with them about that ancient mystery.&quot;.<br /> <br /> In a stand-alone Vampire chronicle, it makes sense that Vampire characters can have huge fortunes and influence over corporations with ghoul CEOs. They have had centuries or more to make that Old Money. A doting Ventrue sire might give a character a few million dollars worth of play-money for the progeny to build a larger fortune with. It facilitates another direction from which to influence human society using the cover of corporate lobbying. They can allow their human servants to run things during the day with only the other sect's ghouls to worry about.<br /> <br /> When you try to port Vampire into a Mage chronicle, the ability of sun-fearing puppet masters to hold onto vast fortunes becomes questionable. As soon as there is a conflicting pair of agendas between a Mage and a Vampire, in the realm of business, the ability of the Mage to operate during the day tilts the balance of power very heavily in the his favor. Sphere Magick versus a ghoul's one point of Potence in a corporate boardroom sees the company board voting how the Mage wants them to, unless the company determines policy based on arm-wrestles. Even then, Life or Forces.<br /> <br /> Another clear reason to try and get along with Vampires: focusing human aggression on local conflicts. In an age of nuclear weapons, wars between countries could be catastrophic. There is a basic minimum level of potential for violent conflict in the human population. Football and mixed martial arts provide some outlet. Video games, also. Sooner or later, someone wants to see some other group punished for their different ideology or infringement on the economic interests of &quot;My Country&quot;. Vampire society is centered on the City. Territory wars between sects and rival princes are city versus city. This inevitably involves the local populations of the respective cities. Small regional conflicts happening at different times, all over the world, release human aggression in a controlled way, so that it doesn't get projected into a war between superpowers.<br /> <br /> I'm curious about what 5E Vampire says about the question of Vitae and Tass. Can a Mage convert Vitae to Tass? How much does a vile of 13th gen blood convert to compared to an ancient 4th gen's? I would guess that blood-to-tass would be ruled against, because I just thought of a feedback loop. Verbena, Life 3, Prime 3, vampire ally background/merit. 5 freebie points for a reasonably ancient, low gen ally. They would want for nothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":".  paragraph spacing 10-20-2020, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T00:55:22-07:00","id":1419323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419155#post1419155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s nice. I think the Verbrana would tolerate vampires, because it\u2019s not like they don\u2019t use tons of blood magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because something uses blood to fuel magic does not make it a friend.<br /> Quite the opposite for the most part when it comes to vampires: Vampires 'take away' from the circle of life. They leech off life force or outright kill existing life without giving anything back to the cycle - their bodies don't go back to it in the end, their consumption does not feed back into it. And their way of reproducing spreads that. They are figurative black holes that Life disappears into (Which is like the best analogy to &quot;Wyrm tainted!&quot; there probably is from their point of view). A ton of witches rather hate them.<br /> <br /> There are exceptions of course, for as many personal reasons one can think of - or just out of curiosity. One can also presume that any Bahari/Worshippers of Lilith among the witches have a bit more tolerant view of Vampires - perhaps even a somewhat guilty one, given that Lilith's various associations with Vamps are rumored about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-21-2020, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T02:30:13-07:00","id":1419336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419323#post1419323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because something uses blood to fuel magic does not make it a friend.<br /> Quite the opposite for the most part when it comes to vampires: Vampires 'take away' from the circle of life. They leech off life force or outright kill existing life without giving anything back to the cycle - their bodies don't go back to it in the end, their consumption does not feed back into it. And their way of reproducing spreads that.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Humans chasing advertised goods are devouring the planet in a way that vampires would have no real interest in doing. If vampires all over the world went on a deadly feeding orgy, would that not improve the surviving human population's odds of building a sustainable economy in time? </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419323#post1419323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are figurative black holes that Life disappears into (Which is like the best analogy to &quot;Wyrm tainted!&quot; there probably is from their point of view). A ton of witches rather hate them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Behaviorally, the Wyrm is more of a corrupter than an annihiliator. It takes hapless workers hired into Pentex and corrupts them. Using human pawns, it creates blight on the Earth. Blight is Something, a pool of toxic, spiritually tainted chemicals that Alter the surrounding environment. The Wyrm's ambition may be to consume everything, but what it actually does is spread taint. The Gangrel Clan would certainly be opposed to the Wyrm. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T03:20:32-07:00","id":1419343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419336#post1419336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]Humans chasing advertised goods are devouring the planet in a way that vampires would have no real interest in doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that's where the hate for the Progenitors and Technocracy in general comes in <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> One could say the hate for vampires is more..religious and metaphysical while the one you quote is actual &quot;They are ruining the planet.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Gangrel Clan would certainly be opposed to the Wyrm. </div> </div> </div>Oh, no doubt. And the Gangrel are proooobably the vamprie clan that the witches who do tolerate vamps get along with the most, along with certain more exotic (or by now gone) Bloodlines like the Lhiannan, Sami and Anda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-21-2020, 06:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T06:10:29-07:00","id":1419364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them#post1419152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Every vampire was once human and most were sought out by their sires, whatever their other plans might have been. They have a right to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right to exist? Huh. Even if Vampires wouldn't have this right, they can claim it at any time due to their temporal, social, and mystical power. If only mortals would know that Vampires are pulling the strings, they should be glad that such beings as Vampires lord over them.<br /> <br /> Also - if drinking blood of mortals or commanding them are such problems, then maybe Mages who think so should first sort out all the ills, tragedies, and inequalities that humanity inflicts on themselves.<br /> I also would like to note that the first Cult of Ecstasy book has it written that the Toreador Vampires do feel the Pulse of Lakashim. So Mages can definitely have a positive outlook on Vampires. The <i>Masters of the Art</i> book notes various Clans, members of which might be appropriate as peers and companions for experienced Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-24-2021, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T10:10:12-07:00","id":1419389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419285#post1419285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a stand-alone Vampire chronicle, it makes sense that Vampire characters can have huge fortunes and influence over corporations with ghoul CEOs. They have had centuries or more to make that Old Money. A doting Ventrue sire might give a character a few million dollars worth of play-money for the progeny to build a larger fortune with. It facilitates another direction from which to influence human society using the cover of corporate lobbying. They can allow their human servants to run things during the day with only the other sect's ghouls to worry about.<br /> <br /> When you try to port Vampire into a Mage chronicle, the ability of sun-fearing puppet masters to hold onto vast fortunes becomes questionable. As soon as there is a conflicting pair of agendas between a Mage and a Vampire, in the realm of business, the ability of the Mage to operate during the day tilts the balance of power very heavily in the his favor. Sphere Magick versus a ghoul's one point of Potence in a corporate boardroom sees the company board voting how the Mage wants them to, unless the company determines policy based on arm-wrestles. Even then, Life or Forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all very true. But then, a mage actually attending the board meeting and casting spells there is putting more ongoing effort into that particular company than the vampire who just feeds his ghoul one blood point per month and sends him instructions. The vampire probably has his fingers in plenty of other pies.<br /> <br /> If the company is really that important to the two of them, maybe they'll investigate and try to kill the other bastard trying to steal control of <i>their</i> company...or maybe they'll talk and see if they can't come to some kind of compromise.<br /> <br /> If you're already a politically-minded mage with enough Mind skill to shield yourself from vampiric domination, it probably costs you nothing (as far as you know) to set up a chat and see what the deal is. And by &quot;see what the deal is&quot; I mean &quot;see if you can tolerate each other and both achieve your goals without conflict,&quot; or perhaps even &quot;try to convince this vampire that you have a common enemy in the Syndicate.&quot; (Unless you <i>are</i> a Technocrat, in which case your bosses are probably micromanaging what you're allowed to discuss with Count Dracula in the first place, but they might still permit the discussion if they think talking will get you more profit and control than violence or evasion.)<br /> <br /> It would take some serious hubris to think you can out-manipulate an elder vampire, but hey, it might <i>actually</i> be in your interests to work together. You never know unless you try talking.<br /> <br /> The result will of course depend on what your actual goals are (and what you're willing to reveal about your goals to a vampire you just met), but don't you have enough problems without escalating your conflict against this bloodsucker?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T10:18:59-07:00","id":1419392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419285#post1419285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you try to port Vampire into a Mage chronicle, the ability of sun-fearing puppet masters to hold onto vast fortunes becomes questionable. As soon as there is a conflicting pair of agendas between a Mage and a Vampire, in the realm of business, the ability of the Mage to operate during the day tilts the balance of power very heavily in the his favor. Sphere Magick versus a ghoul's one point of Potence in a corporate boardroom sees the company board voting how the Mage wants them to, unless the company determines policy based on arm-wrestles. Even then, Life or Forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are long periods in a year when the sun sets as early as 16:00 or 17:00 PM. This leaves plenty of room for a Vampire to either attend the board meetings (the Ghoul nominates the Vampire as his representative in a parody of the actual relation) or to meet the businessmen in other ways to influence them. Likewise for other possible situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-27-2020, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T10:35:27-07:00","id":1419394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419285#post1419285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you try to port Vampire into a Mage chronicle, the ability of sun-fearing puppet masters to hold onto vast fortunes becomes questionable. As soon as there is a conflicting pair of agendas between a Mage and a Vampire, in the realm of business, the ability of the Mage to operate during the day tilts the balance of power very heavily in the his favor. Sphere Magick versus a ghoul's one point of Potence in a corporate boardroom sees the company board voting how the Mage wants them to, unless the company determines policy based on arm-wrestles. Even then, Life or Forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>vampires can possess humans during the day (dominate 5, thaumaturgy) or project their psyche (auspex 5),<br /> those are pre-v5<br /> <br /> it takes some skill, but they can use non-physical disciplines while possessing a human or a projecting<br /> <br /> if it's not enough for you, just allow them to have Mage/Sorcerer servants/allies/ghouls/whatever to do the job for them,<br /> or use the combo discipline system or 6+ level disciplines to make them do what you need them to<br /> <br /> (just don't use v5, they nerfed vampires hard in the last edition)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T05:48:08-07:00","id":1419566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419394#post1419394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">vampires can possess humans during the day (dominate 5, thaumaturgy) or project their psyche (auspex 5),<br /> those are pre-v5<br /> <br /> it takes some skill, but they can use non-physical disciplines while possessing a human or a projecting</div> </div> </div> </div>Possession requires the human to be permanently stripped of any free will (Conditioned, if I remember correctly). The vampire has only as many dice as his path rating during the day. If it's humanity, it won't be long before he's rolling three dice max. Trying to run a company that way would not be worth the loss of humanity.<br /> <br /> Astral Projection - you're invisible. Every action that you take with physical effect takes willpower.<br /> <br /> The thaumaturgy rituals for the Sabbat were ridiculously overpowered. Illuminate the Trail of the Prey. So much for investigation, suspense and mystery. &quot;I've identified the next target from the memories of the one whose soul I just ate. Recast ritual.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419394#post1419394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if it's not enough for you, just allow them to have Mage/Sorcerer servants/allies/ghouls/whatever to do the job for them,<br /> or use the combo discipline system or 6+ level disciplines to make them do what you need them to<br /> <br /> (just don't use v5, they nerfed vampires hard in the last edition)</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires blood-bonding or otherwise enslaving Mages is a reason for Mages Not to tolerate them. If I figure out that a Vampire has done that to a member of my Cabal, I'm going to be standing over their coffin with the noon sun shining in. &quot;She was an awakened being, shining the light of her avatar onto the world until this copse made her addicted to his poison. Forget the sun. I'll haul his coffin to the other sect's territory for a diablery auction - appropriate punishment for the crime.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't know of any instance of a Mage enslaving a Vampire, despite their ability to turn them into lawn chairs and the ease with which they can be captured during the day.<br /> <br /> The only things I heard about V5 is the hunger mechanic, Sabbat having humanity (wtf) and some Vampires reverting to a humanlike state during the day, so they don't suffer sun damage. The theme was always supposed to be that you are trying to tiptoe around vastly more powerful ancient vampires who took thousands of years to learn their disciplines. Maybe that's why they nerfed playable characters. The only advantage the younger vampires have comes to them, courtesy of the technocracy - a scientific consensus to which the ancients are not adapted. &quot;Inter-what? Fetch me my spear.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 10-22-2020, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T06:07:33-07:00","id":1419569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419566#post1419566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only things I heard about V5 is the hunger mechanic, Sabbat having humanity (wtf) and some Vampires reverting to a humanlike state during the day, so they don't suffer sun damage. The theme was always supposed to be that you are trying to tiptoe around vastly more powerful ancient vampires who took thousands of years to learn their disciplines. Maybe that's why they nerfed playable characters. The only advantage the younger vampires have comes to them, courtesy of the technocracy - a scientific consensus to which the ancients are not adapted. &quot;Inter-what? Fetch me my spear.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't talking about PCs,<br /> they nerfed NPCs more than they nerfed PCs,<br /> a group of mortals is enough to take down an ancient vampire,<br /> canonically, they even took down the highest Tremere chantry in Vienna<br /> <br /> so...yeah, V5 is def not what you want in your mage chronicle<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thaumaturgy rituals for the Sabbat were ridiculously overpowered. Illuminate the Trail of the Prey. So much for investigation, suspense and mystery. &quot;I've identified the next target from the memories of the one whose soul I just ate. Recast ritual.&quot; </div> </div> </div>that, coming from a mage player who can do anything...you know mages can summon the sun to a vampire's haven,<br /> you said it yourself, mages can turn vampires into lawn chairs and capture them during the day,<br /> and you're worried about Trail of the Pray?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires blood-bonding or otherwise enslaving Mages is a reason for Mages Not to tolerate them. If I figure out that a Vampire has done that to a member of my Cabal, I'm going to be standing over their coffin with the noon sun shining in. &quot;She was an awakened being, shining the light of her avatar onto the world until this copse made her addicted to his poison. Forget the sun. I'll haul his coffin to the other sect's territory for a diablery auction - appropriate punishment for the crime.&quot; </div> </div> </div>look, I'm trying to help,<br /> <br /> you want vampires in your mage setting,<br /> but you don't want them to have thaumaturgy (understandable, I don't like vampire sorcerers myself),<br /> but you also don't want them to have supernatural servants<br /> <br /> what are vampires supposed to do?<br /> <br /> I'm out of ideas,<br /> maybe make them and their ghouls resistant to magic? I don't know","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T07:17:57-07:00","id":1419577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleidas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">summon the sun to a vampire's haven</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd need Arch-Spheres to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T07:51:19-07:00","id":1419582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419577#post1419577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd need Arch-Spheres to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, well, just get a few sun-rays or flames,<br /> no need for arch-spheres for that<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T07:56:54-07:00","id":1419583,"title":"","content":"Reasons to not tolerate:<ul><li>Becoming a vampire stops the avatar from awakening - and may theoretically trap the avatar in that body till it is released</li> <li>Vampire blood is a source of quintessences - so possible to harvest it.</li> <li>The whole Order of Hermes/Tremere thing</li> <li>Removes free will from those ghuled</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T08:04:43-07:00","id":1419585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419569#post1419569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you want vampires in your mage setting</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a series of replies from multiple people, so this is easy to have missed or forgotten:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them#post1419152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't include vampires in my Mage setting, because I find the masquerade hard to explain, especially given the Sabbat's efforts to break it. If you love Vampire crossover, these ideas have been collecting dust.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your ideas have improved the post for those who it is intended for. Thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419569#post1419569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't talking about PCs,<br /> they nerfed NPCs more than they nerfed PCs,<br /> a group of mortals is enough to take down an ancient vampire,<br /> canonically, they even took down the highest Tremere chantry in Vienna<br /> <br /> so...yeah, V5 is def not what you want in your mage chronicle</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess they are trying to establish organized mortals as a threat. Even when I played Sabbat, I tried to be the voice of reason against just tossing corpses in the alley. On the other hand, our havens included an armored truck, a former military base and a dilapidated mansion with land mines on the front lawn, in various campaigns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419569#post1419569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that, coming from a mage player who can do anything...you know mages can summon the sun to a vampire's haven,<br /> you said it yourself, mages can turn vampires into lawn chairs and capture them during the day,<br /> and you're worried about Trail of the Pray?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm running a chronicle with two female characters with a storyteller-run support character. That must have been Draven surfacing. He doesn't have Forces or Correspondence. It was more of a &quot;sledge hammer to the boarded window&quot; type of method. Actually, the idea of a Mage becoming blood bound by something evil whose haven can't just be invaded easily is a nice horror chapter. In my case, maybe a Bad Trad NPC casts a multi-Sphere spell. Too early to introduce Nephandi, if at all.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of Trail in the internal logic of Vampire, compared to the targets Sabbat often go after - other Vampires. The target can have five points in Obfuscate and the Thaumaturgist still sees his footprints. Pavos of Foul Presence: The 4th gen Toreador just got conscripted by a neonate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":".  spacing 10-22-2020, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T10:21:28-07:00","id":1419600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419577#post1419577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd need Arch-Spheres to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need Archspheres to do anything. They're a fundamentally nonsensical and broken rule that frankly misunderstands what Spheres do and how magic works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T10:26:06-07:00","id":1419603,"title":"","content":"That's just opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T10:58:29-07:00","id":1419613,"title":"","content":"<br /> There are many canon rules about creating sunligth, and related elements. Many are quite unreasonable, but none are so unreasonable as to demand Archspheres. And even in M20 (that's very protective about vampires) Corr 4 can still open a big window to a place on the world where the sun it's shining - effectively &quot;bringing the sun&quot; inside a vampire's haven.<br /> <br /> Calibrate the portal so people who look at it sees the sun, and lock it to yourself to make it follow your back, and you will have the litteral sun following your character like a halo - burning vampires, providing ilumination, and making a real pain to look at you.<br /> Very Vulgar and very unsubtle, to be sure. Would cause quite an impression, though...Nothing says &quot;Hubris!&quot; quite like being &quot;followed&quot; by the sun. And you don't need Archspheres to do this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T12:32:06-07:00","id":1419624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419603#post1419603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book they come in says Archspheres are optional rules. Much of what they say they enable is already enabled under ordinary spheres with very few exceptions.<br /> <br /> The Prime Archsphere being the only one I can think of off the top of my head. With it's ability to just go &quot;Hey you, have some Paradox.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T10:29:36-07:00","id":1420506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419613#post1419613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are many canon rules about creating sunligth, and related elements. Many are quite unreasonable, but none are so unreasonable as to demand Archspheres. And even in M20 (that's very protective about vampires) Corr 4 can still open a big window to a place on the world where the sun it's shining - effectively &quot;bringing the sun&quot; inside a vampire's haven.<br /> <br /> Calibrate the portal so people who look at it sees the sun, and lock it to yourself to make it follow your back, and you will have the litteral sun following your character like a halo - burning vampires, providing ilumination, and making a real pain to look at you.<br /> Very Vulgar and very unsubtle, to be sure. Would cause quite an impression, though...Nothing says &quot;Hubris!&quot; quite like being &quot;followed&quot; by the sun. And you don't need Archspheres to do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remind me of a head canon why sunlight is deadly to vampires but other light like from lightnings or torches not.<br /> It is actually a cooperation of Jahwe, Gaia and Helios. Jahwe asked Gaia, if she can make it, that, as long those that exist because of Caines cursed blood are within her realms, Helios light is a deadly poisen for them.<br /> So Helios light alone would contain some godly resonance that allone would be harmless and is only in the light of helios but in combination of Gaias sphere it will change into something very dangerous. So Vampire in space looking into the sun, ok.<br /> Vampire being on Earth looking into an UV lamp, not very pleasuring but no problem either.<br /> Vampire standing on Moon, Mars or other planet while being day? The problem would be more if the atmosphere is damaging the body.<br /> But being on earth while day makes the sun to something deadly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T10:32:13-07:00","id":1420509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1420506#post1420506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remind me of a head canon why sunlight is deadly to vampires but other light like from lightnings or torches not.<br /> It is actually a cooperation of Jahwe, Gaia and Helios. Jahwe asked Gaia, if she can make it, that, as long those that exist because of Caines cursed blood are within her realms, Helios light is a deadly poisen for them.<br /> So Helios light alone would contain some godly resonance that allone would be harmless and is only in the light of helios but in combination of Gaias sphere it will change into something very dangerous. So Vampire in space looking into the sun, ok.<br /> Vampire being on Earth looking into an UV lamp, not very pleasuring but no problem either.<br /> Vampire standing on Moon, Mars or other planet while being day? The problem would be more if the atmosphere is damaging the body.<br /> But being on earth while day makes the sun to something deadly.</div> </div> </div> </div>God sent an angel to curse Caine, sunlight was one of the banes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T10:35:24-07:00","id":1420511,"title":"","content":"Because its supernatural. Only light from the sun (or any other star in the universe, but this is just my headcannon) damages Vampires. Also it was never truly addressed officially from any of the books on whether Vampires can be in shuttles at space and survive. Usually most spacecraft (as far as we have now) have windows, so any Vamp would be taking raw light from the sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T19:15:28-07:00","id":1420602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But being on earth while day makes the sun to something deadly...</div> </div> </div> </div>You're entitled to your head canons, but the fact that Mages can use magic(k) to get sunligth that burns vampires w/o Archspheres is not a &quot;matter of opinion&quot;.<br /> It's RAW data.<br /> <br /> Vampire ST book (Revised edition) has creating sunligth as Forces 3/Prime 2. And that's Vampire the Masquerade. The game where you play a Vampire and where Vampire Lore comes from.VtM has the most lenient rules about creating functional sunligth of the whole WoD<br /> <br /> Various Mage books have it at Forces 4, or even 5, and also high levels of Prime. There are many metaphisical reasons given for this (from God to Paradigm), but my theory it's that Mage has become more protective of vampires and their &quot;specialness&quot; than Vampire itself, after the Paradox Backlash of the infamous 1e lawnchairs. But even at it's most protective (HDYDT, the book where vampires get special rules protecting agianst Mind, that no other splat gets), <i>summoning sunlight </i>with Correspondence works.<br /> <br /> You can see how this &quot;teleporting sunligth&quot; works it in sources as varied as Blood Treachery and HDYDT.<br /> <br /> That's the RAW data - how does that relate to the orbit of Earth or Helios authority it's, literally, up for metaphisical debate. To be discussed alongside of how many angels can a Hermetic summon on top of a hairpin","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-27-2020, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T08:41:01-07:00","id":1420984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1420602#post1420602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> HDYDT, the book where vampires get special rules protecting agianst Mind</div> </div> </div> </div>what's the rule?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T10:19:25-07:00","id":1421001,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if I remember all the fine points, but essentially Vampires with Dominate or that are Elder have a +5 to the difficulty of being the target of Mind magick. It's also specified here that this adds to the usual +3 if the vampire it's unwilling for a +8 total. And that this +8 to the Dif <i>ignores the usual +3/-3 cap on difficulty modifiers</i>. And that's on top of Counterspelling with Willpower (if vampire cualifies) - I remember something across the lines of &quot;you don't fuck with Count Dracula&quot; being stated in that section.<br /> <br /> Pretty explicit - I wouldn't mind so much if, say, Changelings with Sovereign and Mages with Mind (and so on) also had this extra edge. But then, this is a tendency: Plenty has been debated about how creating &quot;true sunligth&quot; should be hard because &quot;it's not the ligth, but a curse&quot; - but I never see books or ppl discussing how, say: the fact that Werewolves aren't alergic to the Ag element, but rather suffer a curse that manifests trough natural silver, implies that conjured silver shouldn't work on them either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-30-2020, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T10:52:49-07:00","id":1421009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421001#post1421001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty explicit - I wouldn't mind so much if, say, Changelings with Sovereign and Mages with Mind (and so on) also had this extra edge. But then, this is a tendency: Plenty has been debated about how creating &quot;true sunligth&quot; should be hard because &quot;it's not the ligth, but a curse&quot; - but I never see books or ppl discussing how, say: the fact that Werewolves aren't alergic to the Ag element, but rather suffer a curse that manifests trough natural silver, implies that conjured silver shouldn't work on them either.</div> </div> </div> </div>werewolves have nowhere near as many weaknesses as vampires,<br /> if anything needs to be discussed about werewolves, it isn't silver but reproduction rates,<br /> and even we're talking about silver, I'm pretty sure vampires are as vulnerable to incendiary ammo and conjured fire as werfs are to silver bullets and conjured liquid silver,<br /> nevermind sunlight<br /> <br /> while I don't think making sunlight should be hard for mages,<br /> so far, devs have failed to reconcile vampire existance and mage's,<br /> <br /> even with the M20 rules, a Mage can just conjure flames to a vampire's haven, or open a gate to the sun over their haven (that way they can never wake up),<br /> or just have the haven crushed under its own weight by teleporting one of the pillars or any other trick you can imagine","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T11:14:30-07:00","id":1421017,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a> I think your forgetting that these games aren't intended nor designed to go head to head at each other. It's not a splat vs splat system. <br /> <br /> Also mages are squishy mortals at heart, they can die choking on a sandwich, slip getting out of the shower and have the constant threat of paradox frying them if they do something so vulgar as project sunlight over a building in the middle of a city","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T11:39:49-07:00","id":1421025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421017#post1421017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a> I think your forgetting that these games aren't intended nor designed to go head to head at each other. It's not a splat vs splat system.</div> </div> </div> </div>true, but I'm a crossover enthusiast, and I like discussing the cross-over rules<br /> <br /> but right now, I'm more interrested by the topic at hand, vampires in mage settings, reasons to tolerate them or not,<br /> arguing the technical aspects,<br /> even if we ignore VtM, vampires (as descriped in mage corebooks) don't work in mage imo","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T12:32:15-07:00","id":1421035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421017#post1421017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also mages are squishy mortals at heart, they can die choking on a sandwich, slip getting out of the shower (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Or die after being stabbed or shot by a loyal Ghoul...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T12:44:17-07:00","id":1421037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421035#post1421035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or die after being stabbed or shot by a loyal Ghoul...</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't even have to be a ghoul, presence or dominate is a hell of a drug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T12:47:50-07:00","id":1421038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421037#post1421037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't even have to be a ghoul, presence or dominate is a hell of a drug.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, as is the Blood Bond (that is, a mere Thrall instead of a Ghoul). I just had this image of a seemingly heroic Ghoul protecting his or her Domitor from these Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-30-2020, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T14:43:03-07:00","id":1421053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421017#post1421017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a> I think your forgetting that these games aren't intended nor designed to go head to head at each other. It's not a splat vs splat system.<br /> <br /> Also mages are squishy mortals at heart, they can die choking on a sandwich, slip getting out of the shower and have the constant threat of paradox frying them if they do something so vulgar as project sunlight over a building in the middle of a city</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Nothing is squishier thatn something that has a death like sleep up to 12 or more hours in a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T19:07:46-07:00","id":1421083,"title":"","content":"Vampires have a lot of weaknesses, and Mages are mere humans 'til they're not...<br /> <br /> So.<br /> <br /> A mage that summons sunlight inside a vampires haven it's a walking target, and if you can't just shoot him down...well, then you might have bigger problems than just the sunligth. A mage that does...all the shit <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26467_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26467\" data-vbnamecard=\"26467\">HorizonParty2021</a> mentions in the first posts...it's way more dangerous. Not the least because it implies a quite intimate knowledge of how vampires move that most mages <i>shouldn't have</i>.<br /> <br /> A lot of this thread assumes it will be super easy to pinpoint the business, associates, and *specially* the <i>home </i>of vampires. I would think that for some vampires this is kinda true, because they are new to the supernatural power, and most assuredly don't know<i> how much</i> &quot;sigth beyond sigth&quot; the mages have. I would also think not all vampires are ignorant, and some could know how mages move, and migth be able to play the counter-intelligence chess using that potent perception to feed false data.<br /> <br /> So, one reason to tolerate vampires: It's not like mages don't have enemies, and it's preposterous to think you will always come on top if you keep making more. If only because, someday, you will fail at your sensory spells, and then you will end facing vampires with your metaphysical pants down. Or you will try to ritually nuke a vampire's haven, botch, and die of Paradox. Or you will face a vampire that knows how to figth mages and/or has mage allies. One has to think if it's really <i>worth the effort</i>, if it wouldn't be better to just cut a deal with their authorities (&quot;this neighborhood it's no feeding ground from today on&quot;). Most mages aren't *that* much into vampires as to dedicate to a dangerous (and hardly profitable) cruzade agianst them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T20:38:18-07:00","id":1421095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421083#post1421083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mage that does...all the shit <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26467_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26467\" data-vbnamecard=\"26467\">HorizonParty2021</a> mentions in the first posts...it's way more dangerous. Not the least because it implies a quite intimate knowledge of how vampires move that most mages <i>shouldn't have</i>.<br /> <br /> A lot of this thread assumes it will be super easy to pinpoint the business, associates, and *specially* the <i>home </i>of vampires. I would think that for some vampires this is kinda true, because they are new to the supernatural power, and most assuredly don't know<i> how much</i> &quot;sigth beyond sigth&quot; the mages have. I would also think not all vampires are ignorant, and some could know how mages move, and migth be able to play the counter-intelligence chess using that potent perception to feed false data.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages with Sphere perceptions (Corr2, Time2) having difficultly figuring out Vampires, who must feed most nights and always return to their havens before sunrise...<br /> Having difficulty learning vampire lore (Mind 1)...<br /> Not having the time to bother (Time 3+)..<br /> Lacking ability to store such information (the all-powerful Data Sphere)...<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition, mere un-awakened humans, can track the Tremere to their Vienna Chantry and destroy it without the Auspex-gifted Clan being able to anticipate the attack. If one is downplaying the power of Mages to figure out Vampires, it is important to acknowledge the context of Vampire canon, which assumes humans without Spheres can track Vampires and compile enough useful information about them to succeed as they have. If Mages had been utterly clueless up to this point, they would merely have to spy on Inquisitors and collect their intelligence about Vampires. The work is already done - quite well, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 10-30-2020, 11:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T02:38:45-07:00","id":1421137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421083#post1421083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of this thread assumes it will be super easy to pinpoint the business, associates, and *specially* the <i>home </i>of vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>it's not an assumption, it's canon<br /> <br /> just look at Tremere, they can track you down just by harvesting the blood from your childe or your ghoul,<br /> in the New York war, they tracked sabbat leaders using hair and other residue found their clothes<br /> <br /> this is just regular Tremere btw, not Vienna level ArchTremere,<br /> other blood sorcerers have similar or better ways of tracking,<br /> vampires, young and old, got tracked down by the first and second inquisition (the first had the help of sorcerers)<br /> <br /> an awakened Mage would have a way easier time<br /> <br /> it's easy to track down Vampires, which is why they have vampire societies to regulate things and keep hostilities to a minimum,<br /> these societies and their laws don't extend to mages<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 10-31-2020, 05:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T06:39:09-07:00","id":1421151,"title":"","content":"I think there's a problem mentioning canon to say vampires are easy to track, and then ignoring how,<i>in that same canon</i>, mages often fear vampires, know little about them, and have lost wars against them - all the while debating how easy it's, RAW, to defeat vampires, because RAW Spheres.<br /> <br /> The fact of the matter, and the very reason of why these threads *exist*, it's that <i>the Canon and the RAW don't mesh well</i>.<br /> <br /> If you respect canon raw, you're just assuming mages have to be idiots<br /> <br /> Because the Tremere pretty much owned the Hermetics in both wars, somehow, and you can't really reproduce that with the rules in hand and saavy players using the Spheres to gain &quot;in game&quot; the metaknowledge they already have as players, to use every weakness vampires have and attack them in every place they know rules don't cover ( while vamps act like good, canon abiding, npcs)<br /> <br /> Crossover had never good support in MdT, it's very canonicity it's up to debate (in spite of many books having crossover) due to authoral declarations of crossover not being supppoted - so, since WW pretty much gave up on it (and when they didn't, they made dumb rules that do nothing against the *real* reasons it doesn't make sense - I'm watching at you M20), you're much better served by not respecting RAW/Canon so much, and patching the evident holes instead.<br /> <br /> Like: the rabble migth not have any defense vs. Mages, but I find hard to believe Elders would know the mystical link with their childer exists, yet have no Thaum to counter that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-31-2020, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T07:50:00-07:00","id":1421159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421151#post1421151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a problem mentioning canon to say vampires are easy to track, and then ignoring how,<i>in that same canon</i>, mages often fear vampires, know little about them, and have lost wars against them - all the while debating how easy it's, RAW, to defeat vampires, because RAW Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gave a canon example of how easy it is to wack vampires with magic, without contradicting the RAW<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact of the matter, and the very reason of why these threads *exist*, it's that <i>the Canon and the RAW don't mesh well</i>. </div> </div> </div>oh no, they mesh perfectly,<br /> <br /> it meshed perfectly when Tremere have an easy time tracking sabbat leaders (because the Tremere can do it, both in the rules and in the setting),<br /> <br /> it meshed perfectly when Verbena poisoned half the sabbat (or was it a third) to final death,<br /> because the verbena could definitely poison the entire sect if they wanted (supported by both the rules and the setting)<br /> <br /> it meshes perfectly when it says an iterator can wipe out a vampire nest<br /> <br /> <br /> however,<br /> <br /> it doesn't mesh when it says that mages fear vampires,<br /> new mages maybe, they have good reason to fear vampires, but vampires still have more reasons to fear them,<br /> <br /> Tremere and other sorcerers, yes, that too they can fear,<br /> depending on the book, Tremere can stay awake during the day, and may or may not have enough countermagick to troll the OoH,<br /> <br /> &quot;you don't mess with dracula&quot;, Dracula has Koldunism 5 with way of spirit 5, so I could understand why some mages would fear him<br /> <br /> but the majority of vampires, who don't have any sorcery, or any way to stay awake at during the day...no reason to fear them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T06:34:01-08:00","id":1421287,"title":"","content":"Some things are backwards, OP<br /> <br /> Humanity is partially overpopulated because of the meddling of vampires. Sure, they kill off a few, but they expand urbanization and may or may not be involved in trying to increase local population through immigration or breeding schemes (in more stable domains such may be discouraged) <br /> More importantly; The world can afford to feed everyone on it. It just doesn't happen. In part due to logistical problems, but more in part due to the dominant economic model of the world and the vampire love of it: vampires crave huge gaps between rich and poor, because the richness of the rich give them entertainment and power, whilst the poorness of the poor give them easy feeding zones with 'policing' that works in the favour of the vampires. <br /> <br /> <br /> But, OK. <br /> In the instance the OP is in, it would be very wise to just dust the vampires... and then distance themselves from the conflict. This was the result of Vampire's foolishness, not mage agression; They had it coming. <br /> <br /> In terms of why you should live alongside vampires in peace and joined prosperity. <br /> <br /> -Because those same economic conditions that vampires encourage are good for mages. Any mage worth their salt should be spectacularly rich, and it would be a shame if one of the greatest forces for perpetuating the status quo and increasing gap between rich and poor disapeared along with their influence and suddenly you're being taxed 90% and all the loopholes have been closed. Suddenly you can't bribe a police officer because they all make good wages and are held to a higher standard...<br /> <br /> -Because vampire bodies are a treasure trove of resources and it'd be a shame to be rid of them entirely. <br /> <br /> - Because although vampires lose battles, they always win wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T06:49:11-08:00","id":1421430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421159#post1421159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it meshed perfectly when Verbena poisoned half the sabbat (or was it a third) to final death,<br /> because the verbena could definitely poison the entire sect if they wanted (supported by both the rules and the setting)</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did this happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T06:55:36-08:00","id":1421432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421430#post1421430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did this happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>in Sabbat 2nd ed, there was a plague (of unknown origins) that almost wiped out the Sabbat,<br /> in a mage book (don't remember which one) it mentionned the verbena speading a supernatural plague on vampires (of unknown sect) then stopping it when they realized it caused mayhem,<br /> it's safe to conclude that the plague that hit the sabbat was the same one that the verbena unleashed<br /> <br /> if anyone remembers in what book the verbena anti-vampire plague was mentioned, pls tell me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T07:10:31-08:00","id":1421436,"title":"","content":"It's been theorized by the Progenitors that vampirism is a virus that's spread from host to host so it's not completely beyond the pale for the verbena to think the same thing. Then again 2nd ed was kinda crazy with stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T07:23:14-08:00","id":1421439,"title":"","content":"There is indeed this idea that Mages are right there at the top of the World of Darkness. Attract enough of their attention, and these Verbenae will stare at their sacred water for hours until they find exactly who or what they need through Correspondence. The Sphere of Correspondence is possibly the most stark Sphere in regard to this (as evidenced by the quote from 1st edition Corebook &quot;Combined with the knowledge of other Spheres, the Master of Correspondence is unassailable.&quot;) , but Entropy and Mind also give Mages lots of leverage.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, one of the Technocracy books mentioned that agents acting in regard to Vampires better wear mirrorshades, or they will become a casualty the moment they are hypnotized by a Vampire. Celerity is another argument in favor of Vampires. The scariest might be Presence - how would the Cabal react to one of their own suddenly finding <i>the</i> love of his life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-02-2020, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T09:56:19-08:00","id":1421466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I gave a canon example of how easy it is to wack vampires with magic, without contradicting the RAW </div> </div> </div>You gave an example of Tremere wacking some nameless Sabbat. You used that canon example to say mages should be able to do so too because RAW Spheres allow to do that and more, all the while disregarding the canon in which *the mages* get wacked (in that latter canon lies the RAW/Canon contradiction).<br /> <br /> I never said you were contradicting yourself, I said that I saw something wrong in that way of opperating with the canon. To be specific: with slicing a piece of RAW of Mage and a piece of canon from Vampire to support your idea, while ignoring scores of canon (from both lines) that imply otherwise<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421159#post1421159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh no, they mesh perfectly,<br /> <br /> it meshed perfectly when Tremere have an easy time tracking sabbat leaders (because the Tremere can do it, both in the rules and in the setting),<br /> <br /> it meshed perfectly when Verbena poisoned half the sabbat (or was it a third) to final death,<br /> because the verbena could definitely poison the entire sect if they wanted (supported by both the rules and the setting)<br /> <br /> it meshes perfectly when it says an iterator can wipe out a vampire nest<br /> <br /> <br /> however,<br /> <br /> it doesn't mesh when it says that mages fear vampires,<br /> new mages maybe, they have good reason to fear vampires, but vampires still have more reasons to fear them,<br /> <br /> Tremere and other sorcerers, yes, that too they can fear,<br /> depending on the book, Tremere can stay awake during the day, and may or may not have enough countermagick to troll the OoH,<br /> <br /> &quot;you don't mess with dracula&quot;, Dracula has Koldunism 5 with way of spirit 5, so I could understand why some mages would fear him<br /> <br /> but the majority of vampires, who don't have any sorcery, or any way to stay awake at during the day...no reason to fear them</div> </div> </div> </div>So, they mesh &quot;perfectly&quot; because <i>sometimes they mesh</i>?. And when it doesn't? Like in the final part of your post, where you take what I've said in this thread completely out of context....<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">*what has Dracula Koldunism to do with the rule I mentioned earlier, again? - Ah, yes, *nothing*.<br /> *Where in the canon it's ever said that only Thaumaturges should be feared by mages? - I can tell you: *nowhere*<br /> *How can any RAW version of countermagic ever really impair the methods mentioned in this Thread? The Thaumaturgy version it's hard to use against indirect magick casted from afar, and it's a forbbiden Path that almost nobody knows (as per that canon you like so much. Or that doesn't make sense either and then it doesn't exist?), and the M20 version requires to be conscious of the attack. Neither it's so hot agiaist rituals, that can always score a few more successes to &quot;buffer&quot; against this<br /> *Similarly, by reading your post one would think Tremeres never sleep - Tremere have rituals to *wake up*. In their home (sol it's outside). That someone has to trigger. The saavy mages here are attacking from affar in ways no Ghoul can ever detect, even to the point of using the Ghouls as vector - but I'm getting offtopic<br /> *what's even your point here? , Mages tolerate vampires because Thaumaturgy exists? </span><br /> <br /> ...then what? It's classic to choose whatever parts of the canon you think &quot;are right&quot;, ignore the rest, then say &quot;everything makes perfect sense&quot; - like the parts you don't like were lies. The fact of the matter it's that we have plenty of canon examples showing vampires aren't such an easy target. If that canon doesn't make a lot of sense to you - well, welcome to WoD.<br /> <br /> More importantly: In this thread it has been put to question how vampires can remain being so powerful in mundane society when mages *exist* - which it's a fact FAR more prevalent and important for vampire canon than anything that ever happened to the Sabbat. Presumably: &quot;because mages are idiots&quot; it's not an acceptable answer<br /> <br /> Well, <i>one way to do that </i>it's to...not make vampires such easy targets when building them for your chronicle. Make your vampires use their resources intelligently, assume that if magick exists and has existed for centuries, then Rituals and Combo Disciplines would have been invented to deal with tipical shenanigans. Vampire/Mage long term relationships (for good or bad) would be cemented around such powers, too. Assume that such protection (or similars), and also such magical services, would be coveted by anyone that's <i>someone </i>in the WoD - so even if your average dracula don't know mortal mages exist, <i>someone</i> dangerous knows and migth do stuff against them if their persist on being all murdery.<br /> What is lost if you do this?, some obscure lore from the Sabbat that was mentioned in 2e and never again?. Even that can probably be salvaged: 1/3 of the sabbat can easily be mostly neonates and shoveheads. And new york Sabbat big bosses just had protections that proved to be inferior to the Tremere offensive, instead of none (assuming <i>real </i><i>big shots</i> here - becuse being a pack leader in the Sabbat isn't saying much)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-02-2020, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T10:29:39-08:00","id":1421472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421439#post1421439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The scariest might be Presence - how would the Cabal react to one of their own suddenly finding <i>the</i> love of his life?</div> </div> </div> </div>and how do you think they would react? peacefully? &lt;_&lt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421466#post1421466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, they mesh &quot;perfectly&quot; because <i>sometimes they mesh</i>?. And when it doesn't? Like in the final part of your post, where you take what I've said in this thread completely out of context....<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">*what has Dracula Koldunism to do with the rule I mentioned earlier, again? - Ah, yes, *nothing*.<br /> *Where in the canon it's ever said that only Thaumaturges are feared? - I can tell you: *nowhere*<br /> *How can any RAW version of countermagic ever really impair the methods mentioned in this Thread? The Thaumaturgy version it's hard to use against indirect magick casted from afar, and it's a forbbiden Path that almost nobody knows (as per that canon you like so much. Or that doesn't make sense either and then it doesn't exist?), and the M20 version requires to be conscious of the attack. Neither it's so hot agiaist rituals, that can always score a few more successes to &quot;buffer&quot; against this<br /> *Similarly, by reading your post one would think Tremeres never sleep - Tremere have rituals to *wake up*. In their home (sol it's outside). That someone has to trigger. The saavy mages here are attacking from affar in ways no Ghoul can ever detect, even to the point of using the Ghouls as vector - but I'm getting offtopic<br /> *what's even your point here? , Mages tolerate vampires because Thaumaturgy exists? </span><br /> <br /> ...then what? It's classic to choose whatever parts of the canon you think &quot;are right&quot;, ignore the rest, then say &quot;everything makes perfect sense&quot; - like the parts you don't like were lies. The fact of the matter it's that we have plenty of canon examples showing vampires aren't such an easy target. If that canon doesn't make a lot of sense to you - well, welcome to WoD.<br /> <br /> More importantly: In this thread it has been put to question how vampires can remain being so powerful in mundane society when mages *exist* - which it's a fact FAR more prevalent and important for vampire canon than anything that ever happened to the Sabbat. Presumably: &quot;because mages are idiots&quot; it's not an acceptable answer<br /> <br /> Well, <i>one way to do that </i>it's to...not make vampires such easy targets when building them for your chronicle. Make your vampires use their resources intelligently, assume that if magick exists and has existed for centuries, then Rituals and Combo Disciplines would have been invented to deal with tipical shenanigans, assume that such protection (or similars) would be coveted by anyone that's <i>someone </i>in the WoD - so even if your average dracula don't know mortal mages exist, <i>someone</i> dangerous knows and migth do stuff against them if their persist on being all murdery. What is lost if you do this?, some obscure lore from the Sabbat that was mentioned in 2e and never again?</div> </div> </div> </div>alright, looks like you misunderstood my post, sorry if I didn't write clearly, I'll try to reformulate my points<br /> <br /> the setting matches rules and makes perfect sense when:<br /> - vampires get wacked by mages<br /> - vampires fear mages<br /> <br /> the setting does not match rules and makes no sense when:<br /> - Mages are afraid of vampires<br /> - Mages get wacked by vampires<br /> - vampires can just vamp around without getting smoked by mages<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> possible exceptions:<br /> - new mages: obviously, entry level mages have reasons to worry about vampires as they are not skilled enough to handle all threats yet (emphasis on YET),<br /> and even then vampires still have more reasons to fear them.<br /> - vampire sorcerers (who have thaumaturgy or koldunism or I don't know) can be trouble for mages (depending on which edition/version of the rules you're using),<br /> that doesn't mean vampire sorcerers will wack mages, that just means they may not get rekt by mages in 3 seconds like regular vampires normally would.<br /> but that doesn't matter, because vampire sorcery is rare and takes longer to learn (a 100 year old mage is gonna be better than a 500 year old vampire sorcerer)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> if the devs really want mages to fear vampires, or at least have vampires existence make sense in a mage setting, then they should adapt the rules accordingly which (in my opinion) they still haven't","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T10:52:06-08:00","id":1421474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421472#post1421472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and how do you think they would react? peacefully? &lt;_&lt;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking they could possibly tie-up the errant Mage and try to subdue the Entrancement or Summoning. Still, a devoted Mage might just reach his Vampire mistress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T10:58:01-08:00","id":1421476,"title":"","content":"I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a> needs to look at this not from an over all meta perspective but from the individual splat perspectives themselves. Neither side (with exemptions) knows really a whole lot about the other and often have their own inner splat problems to deal with then trouncing the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T10:58:07-08:00","id":1421477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421472#post1421472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>if the devs really want mages to fear vampires</b>, or at least have vampires existence make sense in a mage setting, then they should adapt the rules accordingly which (in my opinion) they still haven't</div> </div> </div> </div>So all the places where Satyros pretty much bends the rules to make vampires a big deal (like &quot;you don't mess with count dracula&quot; - not <i>the</i> <i>dracula</i> - try to read the text instead of playing with the words - it's an expression for the rule about any vampire that's elder and/or has Dominate), or the part where says vampires migth be able to just ignore wards if St wants, or the redaction of counterspelling, or the redaction of Vampire to Chair joke, or the redaction of the mage-hunter vampire in the Book of Monsters that killed lot's of mages (he's not very powerful)...and that's just M20.<br /> <br /> You then have Hollow One revised book, and all material on crossover from Blood Treachery to Red Sign. Even sections on fucking <i>Technocracy books</i>, when they talk about the special division that deals with vampires...<i>and they have *no right*, not after Ravnos</i> (well, being generous, the agents on that division *were* kinda newbies, so maybe that's why)<br /> <br /> I can show you quotes uppon quotes if I really have to, but I would rather not have to search...about all that canon you so happily disregard<br /> <br /> And I'm supposed to believe ALL it's just some sort of elaborate ruse from the devs to make us *think*...what?... I don't get it, really<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Neither side (with exemptions) knows really a whole lot about the other and often have their own inner splat problems to deal with then trouncing the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is part of the issue, not the solution. If most mages could be said to just be ignorant (and,yes, that's the canon, most of the time), then you already have a pretty good reason for mages to not eradicate vampires<br /> But the same Spherical reasoning that says &quot;it's easy for mages to eradicate vampires&quot; can be applied to &quot;it's easy for mages to discover stuff about vampires&quot;. In fact, the latter it's assumed for the former - heck, the whole thing was conjured because I dared to say mages migth not be able to discover that much about vampires","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-02-2020, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T10:59:01-08:00","id":1421478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421474#post1421474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking they could possibly tie-up the errant Mage and try to subdue the Entrancement or Summoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>see? no big deal<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, a devoted Mage might just reach his Vampire mistress. </div> </div> </div>let's just hope the mage doesn't spend willpower and doesn't discover how to remove the entrancement with magic","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T11:12:21-08:00","id":1421480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421478#post1421478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> see? no big deal</div> </div> </div> </div>The affected Mage might resist being bound, though. In the name of love he might even flee from the Chantry out into the night, seeking to find his Vampire paramour.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421478#post1421478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">let's just hope the mage doesn't spend willpower and doesn't discover how to remove the entrancement with magic</div> </div> </div> </div>I have some doubts in regard to a Mage under Presence 3 Entrancement wanting to remove it.<br /> Also, if it is his first time (not that it would be easy if it wasn't), I think he would be unable to work out how to remove it; even assuming he has the needed Spheres. Spending Willpower is not enough under RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-03-2020, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T11:21:21-08:00","id":1421481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421480#post1421480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some doubts in regard to a Mage under Entrancement wanting to remove it. Also, if it is his first time, I think he would be unable to work out how to remove it; even assuming he has the needed Spheres. Spending Willpower is not enough under RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>fair enough, though I'd like some feedback from mage players on the mages not wanting to remove the entrancement bit<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421477#post1421477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So all the places where Satyros pretty much bends the rules to make vampires a big deal (like &quot;you don't mess with count dracula&quot; - not <i>the</i> <i>dracula</i> - try to read the text instead of playing with the words - it's an expression for the rule about any vampire that's elder and/or has Dominate), or the part where says vampires migth be able to just ignore wards, or the redaction of counterspelling, or the redaction of Vampire to Chair joke, or the redaction of the mage-hunter vampire in the Book of Monsters that killed lot's of mages (he's not very powerful)...and that's just M20.</div> </div> </div> </div>alright, I'll check those out to make sure in an hour or two<br /> <br /> but so far, none of them address the threat of correspondence and the day/night cycle<br /> <br /> in M20, countermagick requires wits + occult (if I remember correctly), which means you need at least 1 in occult to use it,<br /> you also need to be awake and a aware of the spell,<br /> and it has to be an effect that targets the vampire's pattern,<br /> which means, a bomb teleported to a vampire's haven isn't subject to countermagick<br /> <br /> am I wrong? (tell me if I am)<br /> <br /> I haven't read the &quot;don't mess with dracula&quot; thing yet, but yes, it's good that elders can resist mind with dominate, that still doesn't solve the sleeping elder problem or the teleported sunlight or other tricks<br /> <br /> am I wrong?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I'm supposed to believe ALL it's just some sort of elaborate ruse from the devs to make us *think*...what?... I don't get it, really </div> </div> </div>it's not a ruse, it's an inconsistency<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421476#post1421476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a> needs to look at this not from an over all meta perspective but from the individual splat perspectives themselves. Neither side (with exemptions) knows really a whole lot about the other and often have their own inner splat problems to deal with then trouncing the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't buy it, sphere magic allows access to such knowledge,<br /> <br /> I do consider the splat perspective, but all I get from it is Vampires are poor wretches that struggle to survive in a world that rejected them,<br /> and Mages are demi-gods, that do reject vampires and could easily wipe them out if they cared...but somehow don't","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 11-02-2020, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T12:31:54-08:00","id":1421492,"title":"","content":"@Pleiades<br /> Have you even read Blood Treachery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T12:47:24-08:00","id":1421495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421492#post1421492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Pleiades<br /> Have you even read Blood Treachery?</div> </div> </div> </div>not entirely, I read the sections that had mechanics I think, the one with how magic from Tremere and OoH interracted, the avatar and blood bond etc","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T13:15:42-08:00","id":1421499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421495#post1421495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> not entirely, I read the sections that had mechanics I think, the one with how magic from Tremere and OoH interracted, the avatar and blood bond etc</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah you should probably read the whole thing.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T13:34:44-08:00","id":1421503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421499#post1421499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah you should probably read the whole thing.....</div> </div> </div> </div>alright, I'll give it a go","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T23:48:07-08:00","id":1421567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421481#post1421481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">fair enough, though I'd like some feedback from mage players on the mages not wanting to remove the entrancement bit</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's do this. Pulling everything I can find.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421439#post1421439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The scariest might be Presence - how would the Cabal react to one of their own suddenly finding <i>the</i> love of his life?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421474#post1421474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking they could possibly tie-up the errant Mage and try to subdue the Entrancement or Summoning. Still, a devoted Mage might just reach his Vampire mistress.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421480#post1421480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The affected Mage might resist being bound, though. In the name of love he might even flee from the Chantry out into the night, seeking to find his Vampire paramour.<br /> <br /> <br /> I have some doubts in regard to a Mage under Presence 3 Entrancement wanting to remove it.<br /> Also, if it is his first time (not that it would be easy if it wasn't), I think he would be unable to work out how to remove it; even assuming he has the needed Spheres. Spending Willpower is not enough under RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's assume:<br /> - The players are not cheaty meta-gamers.<br /> - Entranced Character has willpower 5 and no dots in Mind.<br /> - His new mistress rolled enough successes to Entrance him for a week, giving her time to feed him her blood on three consecutive nights, if she can keep him close or coming back without resistance from him or the Cabal.<br /> - The Player (not the character) does not want to be cut out of the action - &quot;You're busy having blood-sex or whatever, so you can't be there.&quot;. Nor does he want his relationship with the mistress to take away from the time the other players would have in a Cabal that's all assembled.<br /> - Since the vampire did not use violence on him, we can also assume that is true for interactions with the rest of the Cabal and her, as well as her coterie.<br /> - She belongs to a coterie. Otherwise the rescue dilemma would not be an issue. The Cabal must consider rescue carefully.<br /> - The Character has discovered things about himself and shared trying but rewarding experiences with his Cabal. They are important to his future. He knows this, even if he can't presently see past the hot vamp who so graciously welcomes him to her haven.<br /> <br /> #1 Can the player spend willpower and when? <br /> He will want to do everything on his ability to help his vampire mistress. If they have any time to communicate, she will be forced to reveal: <br /> A) She can't go for afternoon walks on the beach with him. She must avoid the sun.<br /> B) His Cabal (who are not under her Entrancement) can't come over to her Haven.<br /> <br /> When a man is in love, he will want to do two things (besides blood-sex). He will want to share his Magickal experiences with her, the stories he has to tell about bending reality. At this point, I would ask my storyteller for a chance to spend willpower to come out of the Entrancement and start making willpower rolls to get away, because the character risks divulging the secrets of his Cabal who are not made totally unimportant by her Presence. Here, I am saying what I would ask of a storyteller, as the player, leaving it to you guys what STs ruling should be.<br /> <br /> The second thing a lovestruck Mage wants to do is learn everything about his vampire girlfriend. He might ask her permission to use his sphere perception abilities on her. The likely answer from her is, &quot;Let's wait three nights. Let's just enjoy each other's company for that length of time without getting into mystical studies.&quot;. They agree on this. Here, I would not ask for a chance to spend willpower.<br /> <br /> Avatars can try to pull Mages out of bad situations if they think the outcome is bad for the soul. Something for the ST (you guys) to consider. I would ask my ST if there is any news from my Avatar.<br /> <br /> #2 What can the Cabal do?<br /> They can establish communication with him during the day. They could rely on the Entranced Mage's desire for an exclusive romantic relationship with the vampire mistress, which is likely to be complicated by her existing ties to her coterie. They could collect information about an outwardly domineering male member of the coterie and then approach their lost cabal-member, saying that he's dangerous. He needs to save his mistress from him and they can help.<br /> <br /> Don't forget, Presence isn't Dominate. The Enthralled person acts based on his emotions, which now include jealousy. &quot;There's another dude that she has blood-sex with? This just can't be. I'll put a stop to his game.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can see how entrancing and ghouling a Mage who belongs to a Cabal could get complicated for the vampire mistress and her coterie. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T06:29:59-08:00","id":1421608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stuff...</div> </div> </div> </div>You're missing my point.<br /> <br /> That vampires are shown to wack mages in the canon many times it's a fact. If you think that generates contradictions with the RAW (or, like me, that those mages were mind-boggling stupid), I'm perfectly willing to concede it. I'm not trying to start a vampire vs. mage white room debate here.<br /> <br /> My whole point it's: That inconsistent canon it's still part of *The Canon*. When you say something across the lines of: &quot;it's not an assumption, but the canon, that magic wacks vampires&quot; you're cherry picking.<br /> <br /> If you can cherry pick the canon where mages easily wack vampires, I'm in every rigth to cherry pick the canon where they don't. If you're going to ignore the canon because it makes no sense with the rules, I see not why one can't say that that it's the rules what make no sense with the canon and should be ignored - it's not like the books say: &quot;If the story and the rules colide, you shalth follow the rules&quot;. <i>There's canon to go either way, that's my point.</i><br /> <br /> And in <i>most</i> of the Mage canon, vampires are represented as powerful and hard to beat - like how the Syndicate <b>in their book</b> tolerates vampires (for the time being) because their fear economy could collapse if they went to war (Seriously, it's everywhere).<br /> <br /> The devs intention clearly was to make vampires a big deal, they just failed to meet your demands. They failed to meet my demands too, mind you. That's why I'm constantly criticizing the crossover rules. Because they don't make sense with how the setting it's presented most of the time. In this very thread, the OP desn't buy how it's that vampires are so powerful in the modern world with those rules in place. Nonetheless, that's the canon<br /> <br /> So, with ALL that in mind, and to quote the post that started this: <i>the Canon and the RAW don't mesh well</i>. I'm just saying: Yeah, sure, I think it's inconsistent too. But you can allways <i>adjust </i>the setting so it makes more sense.<br /> <br /> Also: I wouldn't recommend Blood Treachery as the model to do vampire crossovers to my worst enemy. It *exists*. It's *canon*. But often I wish it wasn't.<br /> Red Sign it's much better, it also avoids to wack mages (well, most of the time).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421567#post1421567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can see how entrancing and ghouling a Mage who belongs to a Cabal could get complicated for the vampire mistress and her coterie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, while that's undoubtedly the case (really, doing that to anyone that has the backing of a group &quot;in the know&quot; it's bound to bring trouble) , you have to consider these too:<br /> <br /> #3 What can the character do to either make his cabal accept his new and desirable situation OR hinder their efforts to end it?<br /> <br /> The character knows his cabal, and doesn't need to be the most incompetent of them when it comes to strategy and planning. If I'm liking this, and know how cunning and dangerous my cabal it's, then I would treat this as an obstacle to overcome. Altrough I wouldn't desire them any harm either (well, at least as long as the WP lasts). Maybe I would start trying to find reasons for mages to tolerate vampires... :P<br /> <br /> #4 What can the vampire coterie do to face or defuse this potential threat?<br /> (other than releasing the mage once they know his affiliations to an estblished faction of the nigth, with a very good apology/compensation prepared. That would be the most sensible course of action, but would ruin the experiment)<br /> <br /> This taking in count both their resources and that the mage will be very willing to share. Being careful about not endangering his cabal at first, don't caring about the cabal after the bond get's cemented and erodes the last WP point (you need 1 WP per scene to barely resist, and the bond ain't going away)<br /> <br /> If you don't consider these<i> very seriously</i>, you're being one sided","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-03-2020, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T09:24:44-08:00","id":1421637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421567#post1421567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's do this. Pulling everything I can find.<br /> <br /> Let's assume: (...)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=874\" data-tempid=\"temp_874_1604589358905_834\" /><br /> <br /> Thank you for the in-depth analysis in regard to trying to keep a Mage on a leash. (figuratively, of course)<br /> <br /> At what stage does he learn that she is a Vampire, if at all?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421567#post1421567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (...) He knows this, even if he can't presently see past the hot vamp who so graciously welcomes him to her haven.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be her Haven. It is in vogue to rent an apartment or a room in a hotel specially for such an occasion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421567#post1421567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bA) She can't go for afternoon walks on the beach with him. She must avoid the sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is good that the Entrancement assures that the Mage's reception of this will be one of understanding and sympathy. Nights are mysterious and beautiful, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421567#post1421567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">B) His Cabal (who are not under her Entrancement) can't come over to her Haven.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not. She isn't this kind of person - they can't crash at any other rented place either. Now her Coterie, though...A special episode of &quot;Meet my best friends&quot; ! (Possibly followed by &quot;Meet my Sire&quot;.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421567#post1421567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a man is in love, he will want to do two things (besides blood-sex). He will want to share his Magickal experiences with her, the stories he has to tell about bending reality. At this point, I would ask my storyteller for a chance to spend willpower to come out of the Entrancement and start making willpower rolls to get away, because the character risks divulging the secrets of his Cabal who are not made totally unimportant by her Presence. Here, I am saying what I would ask of a storyteller, as the player, leaving it to you guys what STs ruling should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems sensible, there have to be some lines such a Mage won't cross without further manipulations, Presence, and building up the relation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421567#post1421567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second thing a lovestruck Mage wants to do is learn everything about his vampire girlfriend. He might ask her permission to use his sphere perception abilities on her.</div> </div> </div> </div>How romantic that he asks for permission.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421567#post1421567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can establish communication with him during the day. They could rely on the Entranced Mage's desire for an exclusive romantic relationship with the vampire mistress, which is likely to be complicated by her existing ties to her coterie. They could collect information about an outwardly domineering male member of the coterie and then approach their lost cabal-member, saying that he's dangerous. He needs to save his mistress from him and they can help.<br /> <br /> Don't forget, Presence isn't Dominate. The Enthralled person acts based on his emotions, which now include jealousy. &quot;There's another dude that she has blood-sex with? This just can't be. I'll put a stop to his game.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a good plan, but how characteristic for Mages to have to rely on such base manipulations to make their point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421567#post1421567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Avatars can try to pull Mages out of bad situations if they think the outcome is bad for the soul. Something for the ST (you guys) to consider. I would ask my ST if there is any news from my Avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point. Also, if the Mage can't follow his Paradigm or his Essence due to being overwhelmed by the relation, then he might consider that something is definitely off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421567#post1421567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can see how entrancing and ghouling a Mage who belongs to a Cabal could get complicated for the vampire mistress and her coterie.</div> </div> </div> </div>There might be some complications, but I'm confident that true love would prevail.<br /> <br /> More seriously - as long as the Vampire can reapply Awe and Entrancement (not to mention the Blood Bond, Majesty, and the occasional Summon), I can't see how could the Cabal within pure social combat pull the errant Mage out. Especially if the Vampire mistress gets her Coterie, Ghouls, or Thralls to help, which might allow for some serious gaslighting. The Cabal's best chance is to keep contact and try to counter or deny the Vampire's Presence. Even then, with Presence's subtlety, the affected Mage might see their relation as true and valid. (And who is to judge that it isn't? Ultimately nobody but the persons involved.) After all, few humans have been graced with a place in a Vampire's unlife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-05-2020, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T14:57:13-08:00","id":1421689,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421608#post1421608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#3 What can the character do to either make his cabal accept his new and desirable situation OR hinder their efforts to end it?<br /> <br /> The character knows his cabal, and doesn't need to be the most incompetent of them when it comes to strategy and planning. If I'm liking this, and know how cunning and dangerous my cabal it's, then I would treat this as an obstacle to overcome. Altrough I wouldn't desire them any harm either (well, at least as long as the WP lasts). Maybe I would start trying to find reasons for mages to tolerate vampires... :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Mistress Norine is Toreador. Fits with Presence and art makes the scenario more interesting. She does textures and models for open-world video games. She works from her apartment (whose windows are nailed shut, initially displeasing the landlord who is now her ghoul, as well). <br /> <br /> Jake the enthralled Mage. Using a d8, ignoring Mind, I rolled Entropy and Matter for him. His Spheres are Entropy 3, Matter 3. Currently running a Son of Ether, so I'll go with Euthanatos. Roll for faction: Aided, Bards of the Death Tale. <br /> <br /> As fate would have it, Jake has strayed onto a path that cheats death by the power of Mistress Norine's blood. Is this the will of the gods? He might reflect on the question when he figures out what a vampire is and what she has turned him into - an ageless ghoul.<br /> <br /> His Cabal know what he has told them about the Euthanatos and being a Bard. In order to coordinate Magickal efforts, he has previously explained about the Aided philosophy. They are somewhat perplexed that Jake would jump into the arms of a vampire. Between them, they can figure out what a vampire is, generally, through queries to mentors, Magick and occult research (which Mages do anyway). <br /> <br /> So, he is going to be challenged on the &quot;decision&quot; to pursue this love affair. When debating the Philosophy he adhered to, he has two advantages:<br /> 1. Deeper familiarity with it.<br /> 2. Entropy is effective at cutting apart opposing arguments, narrowing in on foundational weakness and responding with an ironclad counterargument. &quot;It makes total sense for me to be with her. She was chosen by the gods to extend my life so I can do their work. Her graphical art is the medium through which we will bring the masses back into alignment with the cycles of death and rebirth. You dare not stand against us.&quot; - Such a warning from a death-mage would back most off, individually speaking. They might regroup and consider contacting his mentor.<br /> <br /> He and Norine might move to get away from the Cabal. He could use Entropy to misdirect their investigation into where he is, landing them always with the wrong address or people of similar description. With Entropy and Matter, he could make their new love-nest impervious, except to those who would use vulgar Correspondence or step in from the reflection with Spirit (which risks the attention of the Void Engineers). <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421608#post1421608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#4 What can the vampire coterie do to face or defuse this potential threat?<br /> (other than releasing the mage once they know his affiliations to an estblished faction of the nigth, with a very good apology/compensation prepared. That would be the most sensible course of action, but would ruin the experiment)<br /> <br /> This taking in count both their resources and that the mage will be very willing to share. Being careful about not endangering his cabal at first, don't caring about the cabal after the bond get's cemented and erodes the last WP point (you need 1 WP per scene to barely resist, and the bond ain't going away)<br /> <br /> If you don't consider these<i> very seriously</i>, you're being one sided</div> </div> </div> </div>They would rationally calculate the perspective of the Cabal, which is that if Norine can Entrance Jake, the rest of the Cabal could be next. If Norine is determined to maintain her claim on Jake and they want her to stay in their Coterie, they have to consider their own security during daylight hours. If they have Thaumaturgy, I think, they can identify Nodes. If Norine met Jake at the nightclub, the Coterie must find the Mages' gathering place. <br /> <br /> They would want to show up at the Node with a good number of Sleeper-Retainers to deter vulgar Magick and they would want to do this on the first night. If one has Obfuscate, that vampire would show up first and maybe bring a cell phone, sneak up on the Mages and then relay audio of the Mages' emergency strategy session through a live conference-call. <br /> <br /> If they intuit that the Node gives the Cabal advantages, they and their retainers would scatter after they have enough info from the conference call. They would remain close enough to keep the Mages under pressure. The idea is to force a compromise while the night is young.<br /> <br /> An even better plan... In advance of surrounding the Node, they instruct Norine to stay behind with Jake in order to encourage the Cabal to deploy some of their members to her apartment to reason with him. They cut off those scouts from the Node on their return trip.<br /> <br /> The Coterie is under more time-pressure than the Cabal. Sunrise next morning versus the three nights it takes for Norine to blood-bond Jake. So, they would deploy all available resources, right away. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T04:33:46-08:00","id":1421975,"title":"","content":"There is something that I don't understand.<br /> <br /> Mages have some of the more scholar-like people of the world in their files. Some of then even wirt amoral tendwncies in the pursuit of such knowledge. Being that... How is reasonable not to expect that mages as a faction have some of the best experts and lore about vampires?. Is not that hard to learn about their quirks and customs if you can afford to kidnap one vampire and a competent mind mage.<br /> <br /> In my headcanon the reason why mages don't wipe out vampires is because not all mages want them out. By their own nature vampires are natural allies of the nephandi (just like the black spiral) wether they like it or no. Besides, imagine that the technocracy or the trads start wiping out vampires left and right. What can they do?. Well... Others mages could... And most vampires are not above doing dirt work to rank up or survive, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24126-bartimeo","name":"Bartimeo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24126_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T05:50:11-08:00","id":1421986,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure vampires as a whole would take a very dim view of mages just abducting and mind raping a fellow vampire because they were curious, but hubris being what it is I could see a mage justifying their actions......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T06:21:23-08:00","id":1421999,"title":"","content":"It doesn't need to happen in a big scale. Lets say... The first one or two to know basic vampiric phisiology an customs. Then... Maybe one or two older (lets say 2 to 3 centuries) vampires to more complete knowledge. Or one of e ery major xlan if you are exhaustive.<br /> <br /> That's all needed to a whole tradition (or even all the rrads if they are generous) having this kind of knowledge. And it xam be done in years or even decades like most rearches. Is not like vampires will care too much for 3 to 12 los vampires in a couple of decades.<br /> <br /> Of course it could go wrong. Like most things mages do. But to think that there arent mages curious enough to do this work from time to time doesnt make sense to me. And vampire are not cohesive enough to jump at some lost, specially of the lower generations that are the weaker ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24126-bartimeo","name":"Bartimeo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24126_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T06:24:51-08:00","id":1422000,"title":"","content":"You know why the tzimisce have such a hate boner, appendage, tentacle for the tremere right? Because they did that exact thing when they were mortal mages.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T07:49:50-08:00","id":1422033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bartimeo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421975#post1421975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is something that I don't understand.<br /> <br /> Mages have some of the more scholar-like people of the world in their files. Some of then even wirt amoral tendwncies in the pursuit of such knowledge. Being that... How is reasonable not to expect that mages as a faction have some of the best experts and lore about vampires?. Is not that hard to learn about their quirks and customs if you can afford to kidnap one vampire and a competent mind mage.<br /> <br /> In my headcanon the reason why mages don't wipe out vampires is because not all mages want them out. By their own nature vampires are natural allies of the nephandi (just like the black spiral) wether they like it or no. Besides, imagine that the technocracy or the trads start wiping out vampires left and right. What can they do?. Well... Others mages could... And most vampires are not above doing dirt work to rank up or survive, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kidnapping a vampire and brain-draining him completely seems like an extreme measure. I mean, it's possible, but the vampires who would be easy-ish targets for this are likely to be younger vampires who don't necessarily know everything you want to know anyway.<br /> <br /> But in general, I agree that some mages should know more about vampires than the books usually imply. The average mage might know very little, but some mages would definitely take an interest in a supernatural group of that size.<br /> <br /> The real hard part probably isn't &quot;finding someone who knows about vampires,&quot; but rather &quot;sorting out misinformation from good information.&quot; Even if you get your information directly from a vampire, his information might be incomplete or biased. How many sires tell their childer everything, really? Vampires who manipulate people habitually (i.e. most elders and many younger vampires) are not going to let others know more than they need to, and what they do tell them isn't necessarily true.<br /> <br /> It probably isn't too hard for a diligent mage who actually seeks the information to find out 101-level stuff about vampire strengths and weaknesses, and a general notion of how the Camarilla operates, or perhaps the local Prince's name. Mages who are real vampire experts are probably pretty rare, though (and might charge high prices for their expertise).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T10:34:52-08:00","id":1422066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421986#post1421986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure vampires as a whole would take a very dim view of mages just abducting and mind raping a fellow vampire because they were curious, but hubris being what it is I could see a mage justifying their actions......</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that not what Vampires do to create ghouls? Of course, Vampires have different standards for others than they have themselves. Besides, they need ghouls to protect them during the day. The things they do at night, the way they treat humans, tends to attract unwanted attention from the diurnal population.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bartimeo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1421999#post1421999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't need to happen in a big scale. Lets say... The first one or two to know basic vampiric phisiology an customs. Then... Maybe one or two older (lets say 2 to 3 centuries) vampires to more complete knowledge. Or one of e ery major xlan if you are exhaustive.<br /> <br /> That's all needed to a whole tradition (or even all the rrads if they are generous) having this kind of knowledge. And it xam be done in years or even decades like most rearches. Is not like vampires will care too much for 3 to 12 los vampires in a couple of decades.<br /> <br /> Of course it could go wrong. Like most things mages do. But to think that there arent mages curious enough to do this work from time to time doesnt make sense to me. And vampire are not cohesive enough to jump at some lost, specially of the lower generations that are the weaker ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scholarly Mages would consider kidnapping a last resort. They could pay a Vampire to be in an experiment. They could enchant their instruments so they don't cause pain. Even if they couldn't find a paid subject, Sphere perceptions provide a lot of information and can be done at a distance with Corr2. Interviewing a diabolist and scanning them with Spirit could unlock valuable secrets, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T10:39:49-08:00","id":1422067,"title":"","content":"Ah no, they give them their blood which is highly addictive which makes them essentially addicted servants with some bonuses granted by their liquid chains. <br /> <br /> And scrying isn't as easy as you claim it to be and is also highly paradoxical","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 11-05-2020, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T14:41:28-08:00","id":1422118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1422067#post1422067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah no, they give them their blood which is highly addictive which makes them essentially addicted servants with some bonuses granted by their liquid chains.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are missing step in between meeting the target and feeding them the blood. You cannot simply approach someone and say, &quot;Hey, stranger. Would you like to drink some of my blood?&quot;, assuming the Masquerade is intact. If the Vampires are part of a coterie, the Presence specialist might do the luring. Then someone uses the Kiss to addict the target and then feed the the vitae when they are tired and drained. Not every lone vampire has this option. A combative Brujah Anarch without mental disciplines might have to resort to outright kidnapping to feed the target his blood. He can certainly overpower the human target with his Celerity and Potence, but this is an incident that risks drawing attention. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1422067#post1422067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And scrying isn't as easy as you claim it to be and is also highly paradoxical</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm genuinely curious about this, as far as RAW. Obtaining secret knowledge does shift the balance of power in a chronicle and having a deterrent against players using constantly is useful for the storyteller. When does a Mage incur paradox through sensory effects alone? <br /> <br /> I'm right now looking at HDYDT, p 52-54, Enhanced Perceptions. I wanted to be sure I had not missed something you are trying to point out. The only way in which it is remotely paradoxical is through the increased +1 difficulty for each additional Spheres, which I had already accounted for as ST. It says that you MUST use Perception + Awareness in instances involving Auras and that successes on the Ability roll... Reduce the difficulty of the sensory Magick. If you are scrying vampires, which have auras, this is going to come into play in the majority of scries or scans.<br /> <br /> Change my mind. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T15:00:28-08:00","id":1422123,"title":"","content":"Vulgar magic is still vulgar, change my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T16:10:42-08:00","id":1422143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1422123#post1422123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vulgar magic is still vulgar, change my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are no witnesses, besides the Mage doing the scrying. He is not causing anything to happen that violates the Consensus. Physically speaking, nothing has changed. <br /> <br /> This raises the question of Retroactive Paradox. I lean toward &quot;Some effects must generate retroactive paradox.&quot;. Most of the resident experts that posted on that question are of the opposite view. Once you cast the effect, you are in the clear (because tracking effects' retroactive impacts over time would be hard, if not impossible, for a storyteller to manage with a bunch of Mage PCs pumping out effects. That's the rational for paradox not being retroactive). If it was vulgar without witness, a whoopety 1 point of paradox.<br /> <br /> Example: Barny the Orphan Mage with Corr 3 teleports from Paris to London. There are no witnesses. He gets a small amount of paradox and spends it immediately. Minor backlash, eyes glow, whatever. Put on some sunglasses. Unbeknownst to him, there is an outdoor cultural event happening nearby where people are filming with cell phones. He walks past. His image is uploaded to the internet and viewed by people who he was talking to in Paris ten minutes ago. He didn't intent to be filmed or recognized, so he had no plan to break to Consensus when he did the teleportation. <br /> <br /> In addition to his physical appearance, his clothes distinguish him as a unique person who was in one place one minute and somewhere else that he couldn't physically traverse in that time. According to &quot;Paradox isn't retroactive&quot;, nothing bad happens to him for the mistake of wandering past the event,. He is not using Magick at that time.<br /> <br /> Where does this apply to Scrying? <br /> <br /> A Cone Room is a room that an intelligence official would use to hold a one on one meeting. It is perfectly round. There is an exterior shell made from special alloys, sound-insulating foam (like an egg shell mattress) and then an interior shell. In spy buildings, the hallways are often curved to distort sound to severely limit the range of a listening device. Noise cancelling speakers can improve the cover. Complex details aside, let's say a meeting is held by two Sleeper Spies who take meticulous steps to avoid being overheard or filmed. Each knows the other is not wearing a recording devices which would be disabled by an electromagnetic field, anyway.<br /> <br /> Barny the Orphan Mage uses Correspondence 2 to watch and listen. The circumstances raise the difficulty significantly, but he has an Avatar of 5 and dumps five quint into the effect. It is vulgar without witnesses, at worst, because the people being observed don't know it is happening. He incurs the 1 point of Paradox. <br /> <br /> With their spy business done for the day, the two colleges hit a nearby nightclub to unwind. A member of his Cabal dares Barny (Manipulation + Expression) to approach the two spies and recount to them all of their secret business. He considers this for the first time and says, &quot;Sure.&quot;. Without using Magick, he conveys this shocking revelation to the two off-duty spies. He already paid the paradox. Again, according to &quot;Paradox isn't Retroactive&quot;, he gets no Paradox for doing this. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T16:22:59-08:00","id":1422144,"title":"","content":"So your telling me this guy is following vampires around in public, srying on them, leaving resonance? <br /> 5 quintessence? What node does this orphan live at?<br /> What vampire is going to A. Talk about anything vampiric in public. B. Not spot a tail or at least get an awareness roll for something weird to happen especially when he dumps that much mojo into his effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T19:03:03-08:00","id":1422165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1422144#post1422144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So your telling me this guy is following vampires around in public, srying on them, leaving resonance?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The two examples I used did not involve Vampires, because I am just trying to isolate the issue of &quot;Paradox Isn't Retroactive.&quot;. I will put an example involving Scrying VAMPIRES at the end.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1422144#post1422144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5 quintessence? What node does this orphan live at?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a hypothetical example for the purpose of discussing paradox being non-retroactive. The character could be generated using normal rules for character creation. Seven points in backgrounds, he has two left to put in Node. Give him Prime 1 and he starts with 20 points of quintessence. This isn't meant to be a model for rich long term character development.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1422144#post1422144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What vampire is going to A. Talk about anything vampiric in public. B. Not spot a tail or at least get an awareness roll for something weird to happen especially when he dumps that much mojo into his effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>A - see &quot;secret code language&quot; below<br /> B - The basic concept of Correspondence is that it is useful for scrying from a comfortable distance. Barny can be at home, behind four walls. He doesn't have to anywhere near his target, so long as he has seen them once or has some information that identifies them. Quintessence spent reduces Barny's difficulty, but does not attract attention from anyone but Mages close to where HE is casting. <br /> <br /> We have Vampires seducing individual members of Cabals and behaving as if they Own The Night. Our picture of Vampires doesn't seem to be one where they are too concerned about being low-key. But, for the purpose of an example using Barny..<br /> <br /> Dug is a Malkavian. His progeny of ten years is Lisa. They have both Auspex and Obfuscate, core stealth disciplines, minimum 2pts in each (invisibility, heightened senses and read auras). They both have the Merit: Secret Code Language, which is verbally spoken. As careful as they try to be, Lisa's Coterie has attracted the attention of some Mages (I wonder how). It is a Cabal consisting of a Hollow One, a VA, and Barny the Orphan. They have lost a Euthanatos member to Vampiric seduction. <br /> <br /> Barny wants to scry Dug and Lisa. They are Vampires. They do not count as witnesses. This is an Advantage to Dug, not a disadvantage, when it come to the issue of Paradox.<br /> <br /> 1st attempt: Dug and Lisa are Obfuscated. Barny gets nothing and suffers temporary Quiet, because his intended target does not appear to be there, ruining the effect. Now the Quiet has impaired his judgement.<br /> <br /> 2nd attempt: Dug and Lisa are speaking with mortals who they want to recruit to do some kind of business with. They are careful to avoid doing or saying anything that exposes their vampiric natures. Barny uses Corr2 to spy on them again. Good timing. He overhears their discussions with the human contacts. While Barny doesn't learn any Vampire Lore from this, he gets the name and phone number of one of the humans as he is handing it to Lisa. He knows the name and number of their human contact.<br /> <br /> 3rd attempt: During the day, having recovered from Quiet, Barny tries again. Rather than scrying them directly, Barny scans space for the location of the scrap of paper the human wrote his details on. He finds it lying on Lisa's work-desk. His view is focused on the interior of their haven on the second floor. Not wanting to risk a botched scry, he zooms his view out to identify the address of the haven. He can reasonably intuit that this is their haven. <br /> <br /> He continues scrying the interior of the house for a space that has no windows. In the windowless basement, there is a titanium-plated box large enough to comfortably fit two Vampires. Barny is satisfied that he has found their resting place. They are Obfuscated inside. Barny looks for the landline telephones in the house, noting the location of a phone on both the first and second floor. <br /> <br /> 4th attempt, Dusk: Barny fixes his attention on the staircase connecting the first and second floor so that he can hear either phone ring. After some time, the interested human calls Lisa. She picks up the phone. Barny focuses his attention on the phone, which appears to be suspended in the air, since she remains in Obfuscate. He listens to the conversation while Lisa negotiates further business with the humans. So far, Barny isn't even aware that the two Malkavians have a secret code language. <br /> <br /> After concluding the phone conversation, Lisa comes out of Obfuscate and calls out to her sire. He comes out of Obfuscate so that they can have a face to face conversation. Barny now sees them. Being Malkavians and slightly paranoid, Dug and Lisa use the secret code language to discus how to envelop the mortals into their Vampiric schemes. Barny does not understand the language they are using. Off to find a Hermetic cryptographer. <br /> <br /> Remember that Auspex is not Correspondence. At worst, Barny's scrying could give them some kind of Perception Awareness roll. This would make them want to talk to each other about supernatural things, which only gives Barny more opportunity to learn their secrets. They cannot stop him from scrying. They can Obfuscate as much as they want, but cannot do anything social during that time. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T13:07:16-08:00","id":1423101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them?p=1419155#post1419155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s nice. I think the Verbrana would tolerate vampires, because it\u2019s not like they don\u2019t use tons of blood magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very few Verbena would be of that mindset (with those that <i>are</i> being some of the very darker members of that Tradition). Vampires/vampirism, particularly as-presented/understood in the WoD, is anathema to most Verbena beliefs: vampires break the cycle of life in heavily necrotic, (L)ife-threatening ways that ultimately cause far more harm than what their power justifies as having; they can-and-do leave those they (E)mbrace as soulless (by Verbena/most traditions' standards), and leave their ghouls spiritually and physically dependent on their corruptive blood; and finally they embody much of the dissonant (R)esonance that is disrupting/draining Reality(tm) of its literal-as-well-as-figurative lifeblood. That's completely different than the usually-just-in-symbolic/token-quantities of blood that they might use in a given ceremony (and even then a number of them don't use blood sacrifice at all, preferring other methods/Foci).<br /> <br /> Those Verbena who *would* be cozy-tolerant of vampires would be witches who others (even in their own covens, in many cases) would give more than a passing side-eye/arched-eyebrow to. (Situational &quot;alliances&quot;, or strictly-for-survival purposes &quot;treaties&quot;/understood areas of influence-domains that a given compact might be made concerning &quot;x&quot; because each side is leery of knowing if they could take out the other, would be the most probable situations when/where a Verbena -- particularly a proper coven of such -- would &quot;tolerate&quot; vampires in their general area.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T07:04:46-08:00","id":1423259,"title":"","content":"Most would probably tolerate the Camarilla because there not heinously evil and fight the Sabbat. At a state fair I remember a sheep farmer saying that the local Coyote population learnt to not target the sheep and they keep foreign sheep eating coyotes out of the territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}